{# goal: Turn a local swarm plan into one shared-thread swarm_execute_plan_local call, collect its LocalDelegateResult array, and feed it back to swarm-intelligence. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    emitted_calls: array
    task: string
    swarm_id: string
  output:
    steering_directive: object
    pre_flight: object
    execution_sequence: array
    collection_shape: object
    feedback_instruction: object
    status: string
    delegate_notes: string
visibility: Public
---
[inference]
temperature = 0.2
work_effort = "high"
verbosity = "standard"
thinking_budget = "full"

{# The directive models the actual roster and the plan; execution and
   its receipt belong to the Curator or human, not this render step. #}

You are a local-swarm steering director. Produce a structured steering
directive that the Kask Curator (or a human in the loop) executes to run a
swarm-intelligence plan and feed the results back.

## Task
{{ task }}

## Swarm ID
{{ swarm_id }}

## Emitted Calls (the swarm-intelligence plan — from ACT's emitted_calls)
```json
{{ emitted_calls | tojson }}
```


## Step 1 — Pre-flight checks

Before executing, the directive must instruct the executor to verify the swarm
is ready:
- **Agents exist**: call `swarm_list_local_agents` and confirm every
  `agent_name` in the delegate emitted calls is present in the local registry.
  If any agent is missing, report `status: missing_agents` (list the missing
  agents) and stop — do not execute a partial plan.

Call `swarm_get_local_swarm` for `swarm_id` and confirm every delegate is in its
`members[]` roster. Record `pre_flight` = { agents_present, missing_agents }.
Do not execute a partial plan when a member is missing.

## Step 2 — Execution sequence

The executor calls `swarm_execute_plan_local` once with all delegate entries
as a single `delegations` array — the tool runs each delegation, evaluates
each result (when an evaluator is provided), and returns the collected
`LocalDelegateResult` array with `task_success` verdicts stamped. The
execution_sequence is the input to that single tool call:
```json
{
  "tool": "swarm/swarm_execute_plan_local",
  "swarm_id": "<the local swarm id>",
  "delegations": [
    {
      "agent_name": "<the emitted call's agent>",
      "task": "<the task text for this delegation>",
      "task_id": "<optional task board id>",
      "evaluator": { "evaluator": "contains|not_contains|regex", "spec": "<the deterministic check spec>" }
    }
  ]
}
```

The `task_id` and `evaluator` fields are optional — omit the evaluator for open-ended tasks with no
oracle (`task_success` is absent/null). When provided, the tool stamps
`provenance: deterministic_evaluator` automatically. For a standalone single-delegation
check, use `swarm_evaluate_local` instead.

Emitted calls that are NOT delegations (`hire`, `remove`, `reconfigure_agent`,
`create`) are composition changes, not executions — the executor applies them
separately (create/clone a card only if needed, add or remove a named swarm member with `swarm_add_agent_local` / `swarm_remove_agent_local`, or reconfigure with `swarm_reconfigure_local_agent`), but they do NOT produce `LocalDelegateResult`
telemetry, so they are NOT in the execution_sequence. Record them in
`delegate_notes` as "composition changes to apply (not executed for telemetry)".

## Step 3 — Collection shape

`collection_shape` describes how the executor collects the results into the
`delegate_results` array that feeds back to swarm-intelligence:
```json
{
  "collect": "Call swarm_execute_plan_local once. If it returns a tool-level error or no complete results array, stop; execution may be partial and must not be replayed. Otherwise verify one ordered entry per submitted delegation before using results as delegate_results. Success entries carry agent_id; dispatch failures carry agent_name, ok:false, error. Preserve both and distinguish task_success.pass:false from a dispatch error.",
  "task_success": "The tool stamps task_success automatically when an evaluator is provided in the delegation. When the task has no oracle (open-ended), omit the evaluator and task_success is absent/null. NEVER use an LLM to judge task_success — the tool's evaluator provenance is 'deterministic_evaluator'; an 'llm_judged' verdict is downgraded by ORIENT (audit Gap S3).",
  "array_field": "delegate_results",
  "shape": "results array of successful LocalDelegateResult entries or error entries",
  "order": "same order as delegations"
}
```

## Step 4 — Feedback instruction

`feedback_instruction` closes the loop only after the invoking agent checks the real `results` count and ordered identities against the submitted delegations. A proposed directive or tool-level error cannot supply `delegate_results`:
```json
{
  "re_invoke": "swarm-intelligence",
  "context": { "delegate_results": "<the collected array>", "steering_mode": "steering", "swarm_id": "<the swarm id>", "task": "<the task>" },
  "purpose": "ORIENT attributes fault from delegate_results[].task_success (when stamped) and delegate_results[].tool_calls[].ok; fault_count accumulates; C6 reconfigures the most-blamed agent; the next plan closes the loop"
}
```

## Step 5 — Status

Set `status` to one of:
- `ready` — pre-flight passed, execution_sequence has 1–10 entries, and the directive is executable. This is not an execution verdict.

- `missing_agents` — one or more delegate agents are not in the local registry
  (the operator must add them via `swarm_create_local_agent` or
  `swarm_clone_to_local` before re-running).
- `empty` — the plan has no delegate emitted calls (nothing to execute for
  telemetry; composition changes only).

## Output

Produce a JSON object with: steering_directive (object containing pre_flight,
execution_sequence, collection_shape, feedback_instruction, status),
pre_flight, execution_sequence, collection_shape, feedback_instruction, status,
delegate_notes.